From: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: preserve WAN1 while programming WAN0

AN7581 exposes two hardware WAN selectors in REG_FE_WAN_PORT. The current
GDM2-loopback helper updates WAN0 with a mask that also covers WAN1 and its
enable bit, which clears any independently configured secondary hardware WAN.

Only WAN0 belongs to this helper. Limit the read/modify/write mask to WAN0 so
future multi-WAN code can manage WAN1 separately.

This is behaviour-neutral for existing single-WAN systems where WAN1 is
disabled.

---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2318,9 +2318,8 @@ static int airoha_enable_gdm2_loopback(struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev)
 	airoha_fe_clear(eth, REG_FE_VIP_PORT_EN, BIT(AIROHA_GDM2_IDX));
 	airoha_fe_clear(eth, REG_FE_IFC_PORT_EN, BIT(AIROHA_GDM2_IDX));
 
-	airoha_fe_rmw(eth, REG_FE_WAN_PORT,
-		      WAN1_EN_MASK | WAN1_MASK | WAN0_MASK,
+	airoha_fe_rmw(eth, REG_FE_WAN_PORT, WAN0_MASK,
 		      FIELD_PREP(WAN0_MASK, src_port));
 	val = src_port & SP_CPORT_DFT_MASK;
 	airoha_fe_rmw(eth,
